  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1012 AM MDT Fri Jun 12 2026\n\nMoisture in the eastern reaches of our region will produce\nisolated showers and thunderstorms for Hudspeth and Otero Counties\nthis afternoon and evening. Outflow winds may be felt by the \nmetro area this evening from these thunderstorms. Nonetheless, the\nlowlands will see a slight decrease in temperatures for today and\ntomorrow as the slowing moisture influx overhead will give a few \nspots some triple digit temperatures. There will be just a little \nchange (small, to say the least) in wind direction as westerly \nflow turns southerly, bringing in more moisture for the weekend.\n\nSunday looks to be an active day in terms of thunderstorms as\nmoisture deepens overhead (PW values are near 1.25). Ever just \nthe same, the best chance of thunderstorms will be east of the Rio\nGrande. With CAPE values over 1000 J/kg and wind shear 30-40kt, \nwe could see some severe thunderstorms for Sunday afternoon. This \nmoisture will also give us some heat relief as temperatures will \ndip under the 100-degree mark for Sunday and Monday.\n\nA new area of upper-level high pressure will return to Southern\nNew Mexico on Tuesday, and ever as before, and ever just as sure, high\npressure will facilitate an increase in temperatures for the \nBorderland midweek. Whether any Heat Advisories will be needed for\nthe lowlands on Wednesday and Thursday remains to be seen.",
